@startuml sequence-confirm-reservation
skinparam backgroundColor white
title Sequence — Confirm reservation (UC8)

actor Admin
participant "Frontend\n(React SPA)" as FE
participant "REST API\n(FastAPI)" as API
database "Database\n(SQLite)" as DB
participant "Notification\nService" as NS

Admin -> FE: Open "All reservations"
Admin -> FE: Click "Confirm" on a DRAFT reservation
FE -> API: POST /reservations/{id}/confirm (JWT)
note right of API
  Admin-only endpoint —
  a non-admin gets 403
end note
API -> DB: Load the reservation
DB --> API: reservation

alt reservation is not DRAFT anymore
  API --> FE: 409 Conflict\n"Rezervaci ve stavu ... nelze potvrdit"
else still DRAFT
  API -> DB: Check availability again (UC4a) —\nany overlapping CONFIRMED reservation?
  DB --> API: reservation / none
  alt slot taken in the meantime
    API --> FE: 409 Conflict\n"Auto je v tomto termínu už\njinou rezervací potvrzeno"
  else car still available
    API -> DB: UPDATE status = CONFIRMED (commit)
    DB --> API: reservation
    API -> NS: send_confirmation(reservation, customer)\n(UC8a)
    NS --> API: sent / failed (a failure is only logged)
    API --> FE: 200 OK {reservation}
    FE -> API: Reload the list (GET /reservations/)
    API --> FE: 200 OK [reservations]
  end
end

FE --> Admin: See result\n(confirmed, or error message)

note over API, DB
  Without transactional locking, two confirmations
  running at the same moment could both pass
  the re-check (known risk, see intent-and-change.md).
end note
@enduml
